From: Tom Plant <tom@tplant.com.au>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: thead: Fix WiFi on Lichee Pi 4A

The RTL8723DS on the Lichee Pi 4A never enumerates:

  mmc2: error -110 whilst initialising SDIO card
  mmc2: Failed to initialize a non-removable card

The card answers CMD5 and offers 1.8V signalling (S18A), but its I/O
rail is wired to the board's fixed 1.8V supply, so the CMD11 voltage
switch fails and every retry times out.

Set no-1-8-v on sdio1 so the core does not attempt the switch.

Fixes: a20241c08385 ("riscv: dts: thead: Enable WiFi on Lichee Pi 4A")
Assisted-by: Claude
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/thead/th1520-lichee-pi-4a.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/thead/th1520-lichee-pi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/thead/th1520-lichee-pi-4a.dts
@@ -175,6 +175,7 @@
 	cap-sdio-irq;
 	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
+	no-1-8-v;
 	non-removable;
 	status = "okay";
 };
